# npm audit ignore list for `task frontend:audit` (and task audit), read by
# scripts/npm-audit.sh. Same convention as .trivyignore.
#
# Every entry MUST carry:
#   - why it is accepted (unfixed upstream, unreachable in this context, ...)
#   - a "Revisit YYYY-MM-DD" date
#
# scripts/check-trivyignore-expiry.sh fails once a date has passed, and
# scripts/npm-audit.sh fails on an entry npm no longer reports, so nothing
# here can age quietly.
#
# Format:
#   GHSA-xxxx-xxxx-xxxx  # accepted: <reason>. Revisit YYYY-MM-DD.

# braces <= 3.0.3, CVE-2026-93687 (high): stack overflow on deeply nested
# brace patterns. No fixed release exists; the fix is micromatch/braces#72,
# unmerged, maintainer inactive since 2025-01. Reached only through the dev
# dependency markdownlint-cli2 (directly via micromatch, and via globby ->
# fast-glob -> micromatch). braces only ever sees the glob patterns that
# select files to lint -- the CLI argument and the ignore lists in this
# repo -- never Markdown content, so triggering it needs commit access and
# the worst case is a crashed lint run. Risk accepted 2026-10-03.
# A braces 3.0.4 reaches us through micromatch's ^3.0.3 with a lockfile
# refresh alone; drop this entry then.
GHSA-vfj7-8cjw-p6xm  # accepted: unfixed upstream, dev-only, repo-controlled input. Revisit 2027-01-04.

# katex 0.16.47, prototype pollution can bypass `trust` restrictions (low).
# Fixed in 0.18.2, but the only consumer, micromark-extension-math 3.1.0
# (inside markdownlint 0.41.1, inside markdownlint-cli2), declares ^0.16.0,
# and on a 0.x line 0.18 is a breaking release; no newer markdownlint pins a
# fixed range yet. katex only renders math to HTML, and markdownlint only
# parses Markdown -- it never calls the HTML compiler -- so katex code never
# runs here. Development dependency only. Accepted 2026-10-11; drop when a
# markdownlint-cli2 release moves to katex >= 0.18.2.
GHSA-238p-pmpm-9mq7  # accepted: unreachable (parse-only), dev-only, fix out of range. Revisit 2027-01-04.
